    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstraction for the shape of a structure such as a multidimensional view, i.e. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>everything but the data itself. A type to be used with cudastf must specialize this template.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The data corresponding to this shape.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Any specialization must be default constructible, copyable, and assignable. The required methods are constructor from <computeroutput>const T&amp;</computeroutput>. All other definitions are optional and should provide full information about the structure (&quot;shape&quot;) of an object of type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>, without actually allocating any data for it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
